# Attachment

The publishing attachment component presents a document link with useful file information and an accessible-format route. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/components/attachment/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use this adaptation for household manuals, installation instructions and maintenance documents. Put the document title before format, size and language. Prefer an HTML version when the information can be presented as an accessible web page. A thumbnail is optional and must not become a second keyboard stop for the same download.

## Structure and behaviour

The content model requires a meaningful title and a real destination. Add file type, measured size and revision only when known. Keep document metadata distinct from live appliance state. A link to view a manual and a button that changes an appliance perform different jobs and must remain separate.

## Home Assistant boundary

This reference does not create a document store, request an accessible copy or download a file. The examples open an actual in-page text preview. Do not show an accessible-format request link unless someone is responsible for fulfilling it; do not publish manufacturer artwork without checking its permission.

